ication that they want  anything else for their lives but that  could simply be because they never  considered that other options might be  open to them  shenyang the only other woman who wanted  something more than what society was  prepared to offer  is dead by the film's end kids may be  satisfied that mulan herself is able to  finally lead the life that she wants  but adults may wonder how much has  really changed  mulan accepting her commission as an  officer in the emperor's guard is  presented as a happy ending  but mulan likely has an extremely hard  road ahead of her  remember the army that she's going to  join is the same one that earlier  in the film reminded its soldiers that  the presence of a woman in the camp was  punishable by death  although the men who fought beside mulan  against bori khan are ready and willing  to accept her as a warrior  there are plenty of other men in the  emperor's guard who don't know her  personally  they aren't all going to be thrilled at  the idea of admitting a woman to their  ranks much less as a leader  not all men will find it easy to let go  of the way things have always been done  in the past and it's probable that at  least some of mulan's fellow soldiers  could decide to make her life  particularly difficult in order to prove  that women have no place among them  mulan was able to earn the respect of  her peers once before  but that was only after she'd previously  earned it as a man  her new career as the only female  officer in the emperor's guard will no  doubt be a tremendously challenging one  but we are sure she's up to the task  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and tv shows are  coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

